    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d338">

                <pb facs="0379" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg345"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mills to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu, Hawaiian Islands</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1897-02-10"><hi rendition="#italic">February
                                10, 1897</hi></date>. (Received February 23.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 198.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 159, of January 27,
                    in which I am instructed to make to the minister of foreign affairs an
                    appropriate expression of the appreciation of the Government of the United
                    States of the honors shown by that of Hawaii to the remains of Minister Willis,
                    I have the honor to say that on the 9th ultimo I addressed a note to Minister
                    Cooper on the subject, and inclose a copy thereof.</p>
                <p>Hoping that my action in this matter will meet with your approval, I am,
                    etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ellis Mills</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d338-a1.xml" xpointer="d338-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
